  "notes": "The most consonant model in this container and the only one built on major-7 / minor-9 soul vamps: ii–V–I and I–vi–ii–V over 4-bar loops, with sevenths and ninths taking three quarters of the extension weight where the parent gives them eight percent. Straight time, backbeat on 2&4, and the two parameters that make it \"relaxed\" are engine-level rather than decorative — `snare.offGridMs` is positive so the backbeat sits behind the grid as the research says, and `velocityTiers` are compressed into a narrow band because the research names a low velocity range. ⛔ `drums.bass808.role` is moved off `bassline`: the research says played bass with melodic motion and minimal 808, so the `bassline` block grows a real part — `independent_riff`, `followRootsProb` 0.5, a 21-semitone register and four passing tones. ⚠ `low`, tracking the research's medium-low: only the Rap-A-Lot lane and era are documented and the paragraph says outright that the parameters are inferred from the label's live-player idiom. The 76–92 BPM band, the tambourine layer, the chord families and the countermelody weights are all INFERRED. ⚠ `fills.snareRollLadder` is off — both fill periods sit at 4 bars, the big fill wins, and the inherited ladder reads no seed, so it writes one identical fill on every one of them. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.3 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.3 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 52 to 51 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 52 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1. ⚠ **The 1-bar phrase length was removed** (was [4,2,1], now [4,2]). A one-bar phrase looped four times carries less entropy than a four-bar phrase, and it is the countermelody it strangles hardest: a counter answers *inside* the melody’s phrase, so a one-bar shape leaves it nowhere to go. Every worst offender on `counter.rs` carried it. ⛔ The previous session recorded this exact mistake and it arrived again from the other direction — distinctness is combinatorial in the shape LENGTH, not in the option count.",
